meta {
  name: Stream run events (SSE)
  type: http
  seq: 4
  tags: [
    smoke
  ]
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/runs/{{runId}}/events
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  The run's event log as Server-Sent Events: the history is replayed first, then live events and `delta` previews follow until the `terminal` event, when the server closes the stream.

  A frame looks like `event: content` / `data: {"event_id", "seq", "type", "actor", "body", ...}`. `body` is the decrypted payload, shown only to the run's own user; `thought` events never carry one.

  A conversational run (`chatRunId`) does not emit `terminal` while it waits for your next message, so its stream stays open: close the request when you have seen enough.
}
